  "summary": "Correlated frames and receipts of one connection with the single owner (--delivery-shards 0: the coordinator is the only producer and the only receipt consumer; net.rs ConnCore, OutgoingState, StalledState and Task, net/tls.rs Task, runtime/sink.rs Sink::try_submit, runtime.rs collect_written and finish_close): the output queue is the transport's only bound on the frames of a connection, a turn offers its receipts in order under one lock and takes no frame while the lane refuses one, the task produces at most one terminal receipt per frame and nothing after `finished`, a task that ends seals its queue so that no frame is accepted and left without a receipt, and every accepted frame gets exactly one terminal result at the core, from its receipt or from the close. Not modelled, and present with --delivery-shards K >= 1: the write reservation of a shard (ShardIoRoute::reserve_write), receipts and subscriber acknowledgements routed to a ShardInbox, a shard as second producer, the wait of finish_close for the shard's detach. Not modelled either: WireProgress, uncorrelated frames, the runtime's bounds that span all connections.",
